{
  "version": 3,
  "format": "story",
  "title": "How does Android build the vendor image?",
  "topic": "aosp/treble/system-vendor-split",
  "genre": "trace",
  "style": "terminal",
  "series": "aosp-treble-hals",
  "series_index": 1,
  "level": "intermediate",
  "tags": [
    "aosp",
    "treble",
    "vendor",
    "build",
    "soong",
    "lineageos",
    "vintf"
  ],
  "cast": [
    {
      "id": "maintainer",
      "name": "Maya",
      "role": "New ROM maintainer porting a phone",
      "color": "#E4572E"
    },
    {
      "id": "reviewer",
      "name": "Dev",
      "role": "Senior build reviewer",
      "color": "#2F6F8F"
    }
  ],
  "glossary": [
    {
      "term": "Treble",
      "full": "Project Treble",
      "note": "Android's split between the framework and vendor code."
    },
    {
      "term": "HAL",
      "full": "Hardware Abstraction Layer",
      "note": "Vendor code that talks to one piece of hardware."
    },
    {
      "term": "VINTF",
      "full": "Vendor Interface",
      "note": "A manifest of the HALs the vendor image offers."
    },
    {
      "term": "vendor image",
      "full": "The vendor partition image (vendor.img)",
      "note": "Chip-specific files, built apart from system."
    },
    {
      "term": "device tree",
      "full": "A phone's folder of build configuration",
      "note": "Holds files like device.mk and BoardConfig.mk."
    },
    {
      "term": "PRODUCT_COPY_FILES",
      "full": "Build list of source:destination file copies",
      "note": "Destination is relative to the product output."
    },
    {
      "term": "TARGET_COPY_OUT_VENDOR",
      "full": "Where vendor files are copied in the output",
      "note": "vendor with a vendor image, system/vendor without."
    }
  ],
  "key_points": [
    "Mark a module vendor: true, or copy files with TARGET_COPY_OUT_VENDOR.",
    "BOARD_VENDORIMAGE_FILE_SYSTEM_TYPE turns on a separate vendor image.",
    "m vendorimage writes out/target/product/<device>/vendor.img."
  ],
  "sources": [
    "https://github.com/LineageOS/android_device_xiaomi_gemini/commit/d24fb6c6f4c9526439ff3db78ed000ddb87db512",
    "https://source.android.com/docs/core/architecture/partitions",
    "https://source.android.com/docs/core/architecture/vintf"
  ],
  "beats": [
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Since Project Treble, Android ships in two halves. System is the framework. Vendor is the chip maker's code.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.box",
          "id": "sys",
          "text": "System",
          "sub": "Android framework",
          "icon": "cloud",
          "at": 0.45
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.box",
          "id": "ven",
          "text": "Vendor",
          "sub": "chip-specific code",
          "icon": "cache",
          "tone": "accent",
          "at": 0.7
        },
        {
          "do": "define",
          "term": "Treble",
          "at": 0.15
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "maintainer",
      "text": "I'm porting a phone. My HAL files must land in vendor.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "define",
          "term": "HAL",
          "at": 0.7
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "HALs belong in vendor",
          "at": 0.8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "reviewer",
      "text": "Then build only that image: m vendorimage.",
      "say": "Then build only that image: m, vendorimage.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "split"
        },
        {
          "do": "term.type",
          "id": "build",
          "cmd": "m vendorimage",
          "out": [],
          "at": 0.5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "maintainer",
      "text": "But how does the build know what belongs?",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "what belongs in vendor?",
          "at": 0.5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "reviewer",
      "text": "Every module tags itself. In Android.bp, one line: vendor true.",
      "say": "Every module tags itself. In Android dot B P, one line: vendor true.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "code.show",
          "id": "bp",
          "lang": "bp",
          "title": "Android.bp (example)",
          "code": [
            "cc_library_shared {",
            "    name: \"libexample_hw\",",
            "    vendor: true,",
            "}"
          ],
          "highlight": [
            2
          ],
          "at": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "reviewer",
      "text": "Old makefiles say LOCAL_VENDOR_MODULE instead.",
      "say": "Old makefiles say local vendor module instead.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "code.show",
          "id": "mk",
          "lang": "make",
          "title": "Android.mk (example)",
          "code": [
            "LOCAL_VENDOR_MODULE := true"
          ],
          "highlight": [
            0
          ],
          "at": 0.35
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Prebuilt files travel by PRODUCT_COPY_FILES: source, colon, destination.",
      "say": "Prebuilt files travel by product copy files: source, colon, destination.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "clear"
        },
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "code.show",
          "id": "before",
          "lang": "make",
          "title": "device.mk (shortened)",
          "code": [
            "PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \\",
            "  audio_platform_info.xml:system/vendor/etc/audio_platform_info.xml"
          ],
          "highlight": [
            1
          ],
          "at": 0.2
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "reviewer",
      "text": "A LineageOS maintainer fixed one of these in a real Xiaomi device tree.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "commit.story",
          "id": "commit",
          "repo": "LineageOS/android_device_xiaomi_gemini",
          "title": "Audio configs copied to system/vendor",
          "at": 0.5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "maintainer",
      "text": "The destination says vendor. Looks fine to me.",
      "visuals": []
    },
    {
      "speaker": "reviewer",
      "text": "It says system slash vendor. That only works while vendor lives inside system.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "commit.story",
          "id": "commit",
          "repo": "LineageOS/android_device_xiaomi_gemini",
          "broke": "The path is hardcoded, so a real vendor partition would miss these files.",
          "at": 0.6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "reviewer",
      "text": "The fix: copy to TARGET_COPY_OUT_VENDOR instead.",
      "say": "The fix: copy to target copy out vendor instead.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full",
          "keep": [
            "commit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "code.show",
          "id": "after",
          "lang": "make",
          "title": "after",
          "code": [
            "PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \\",
            "  audio_platform_info.xml:$(TARGET_COPY_OUT_VENDOR)/etc/audio_platform_info.xml"
          ],
          "highlight": [
            1
          ],
          "at": 0.3
        },
        {
          "do": "commit.story",
          "id": "commit",
          "repo": "LineageOS/android_device_xiaomi_gemini",
          "fix": "Copy to $(TARGET_COPY_OUT_VENDOR) instead of a fixed path.",
          "why": "The variable follows the board, so the path stays correct.",
          "at": 0.6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "The board config can ask for a vendor image. Then that variable becomes just vendor.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "clear",
          "keep": [
            "after"
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "code.show",
          "id": "board",
          "lang": "make",
          "title": "BoardConfig.mk",
          "code": [
            "BOARD_VENDORIMAGE_FILE_SYSTEM_TYPE := ext4"
          ],
          "highlight": [
            0
          ],
          "at": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "maintainer",
      "text": "So the build packs everything into one file?",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "one file?",
          "at": 0.6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Yes: vendor image, under out slash target slash product.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "clear"
        },
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.box",
          "id": "img",
          "text": "vendor image",
          "sub": "out/target/product/<device>/vendor.img",
          "icon": "db",
          "tone": "accent",
          "at": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "reviewer",
      "text": "Inside, a VINTF manifest lists every HAL it offers. The framework checks it.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "define",
          "term": "VINTF",
          "at": 0.2
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.box",
          "id": "vintf",
          "text": "VINTF manifest",
          "sub": "vendor/etc/vintf",
          "icon": "server",
          "at": 0.45
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
